{% layout "layout.glaze" title: "Getting started", current: "/start" %}
<article class="prose">
<h1>Getting started</h1>
<p>With Kiln 0.9.0 or later, build a server-rendered page, add an interactive Ember and call a typed server function. Local modules keep shared code in separate folders. No Node project or dependency installation is needed.</p>
<h2 id="files">Files and modules</h2>
<p>Create this folder tree. A folder is a module; its <code>.kiln</code> files share declarations. Import child modules explicitly and export their functions with <code>pub</code>.</p>
<pre><code>hello/
  main.kiln
  home.glaze
  counter.ember
  greetings/
    message.kiln</code></pre>
<h2 id="a-server">A server</h2>
<p>Put this in <code>hello/main.kiln</code>. The <code>server fn</code> is callable from an Ember; Kiln generates the browser/server transport and checks its arguments and result.</p>
<pre><code data-file="main.kiln">{samples().main}</code></pre>
<p>Put the exported helper in <code>hello/greetings/message.kiln</code>:</p>
<pre><code data-file="greetings/message.kiln">{samples().module}</code></pre>
<h2 id="a-page">A server-rendered page</h2>
<p>Put this in <code>hello/home.glaze</code>. Glazes are server-only pages or components. Their props and styles are checked, and text is escaped by default.</p>
<pre><code data-file="home.glaze">{samples().glaze}</code></pre>
<h2 id="an-ember">An interactive Ember</h2>
<p>Put this in <code>hello/counter.ember</code>. State and <code>on:</code> handlers belong in <code>.ember</code> files. The <code>Counter</code> tag resolves the filename; <code>client:visible</code> hydrates it when it becomes visible.</p>
<pre><code data-file="counter.ember">{samples().ember}</code></pre>
<p>The count changes in the browser. “Ask the server” calls <code>greet</code> and shows its result. Embers run as WasmGC in a compatible modern browser. A page without Embers loads no Ember JavaScript or WebAssembly.</p>
<h2 id="run-it">Run it</h2>
<pre><code>kiln check hello
kiln run hello</code></pre>
<p>Open <a href="http://127.0.0.1:8080">127.0.0.1:8080</a> and try both buttons. <code>kiln build hello</code> makes a native executable; <code>kiln build hello --target windows -o hello.exe</code> builds for Windows.</p>
<p>This project needs no manifest. An optional <code>kiln.toml</code> can select an entry file; see <a href="/docs/reference/projects">projects and local modules</a> for the exact schema, visibility, component paths and module assets.</p>
<h2 id="next">Next</h2>
<ul>
<li><a href="/docs/reference/syntax">The language</a>, its <a href="/docs/reference/types">types</a> and its <a href="/docs/reference/stdlib">standard library</a></li>
<li><a href="/docs/reference/glazes">Glazes and Embers</a>: pages, components, layouts, styling, state and RPC</li>
<li><a href="/docs/reference/projects">Projects and modules</a>: organize an application across folders</li>
</ul>
<p>SQL, ORM, sessions/auth, Wares and the public <code>kiln test</code> command are planned. Follow the current references for working APIs.</p>
</article>
